 "looked_at": "Looked at by the agent on 19 October 2026, before any radar reading was opened: the whole mosaic in true colour beside each rule at about 6 m, four parts at about 2 m, and three squares of 300 m at 0.5 m in true and false colour (near infrared as red). The scene is dry: no open flood water is seen anywhere at these scales; the Sai River is brown and full, fields are green or bare, and light-brown deposits of sand and silt lie in the town and over fields, largest east of the clouds in the north-east corner. Rule v2 calls 1.8 km2 of the compared district water. Its real water is ponds and the reservoir in the south-west. Most of the rest is not water: bare fields in the south-east (near 597764 E, 2256408 N, pale green in false colour, no dark surface), the fresh deposit east of the clouds (near 600884 E, 2262168 N, 69 percent of the 300 m square called water, textured sand and silt with flow marks), and metal roofs and their shadows in town. It misses the brown river. Cloud is set aside, its thin edges and shadows are not. Rule v1 calls 27.4 km2 water: the whole town, the roads, the brown river and many fields.",
 "set_aside_from_the_comparison": "Rule v2 fails on this scene in the way plan section 4 names: bare soil and fresh flood sediment read as water (south-east fields; the deposit east of the clouds in the north-east), and roofs in town. What it calls water is mostly not water, so it cannot serve as the water of the image for question 1. Set aside before any comparison, as amendment 1 says.",
 "rule_v1_left_out": "Rule v1 fails too: it calls the town, the roads, the brown river and many fields water (27.4 km2).",
